# One UI, two targets

`tassel-app` ships the same Compose UI to desktop (JVM) and web (wasmJs).

- Shared UI lives in `commonMain`. Only file pickers, windowing, and
  engine wiring go in `desktopMain`/`wasmJsMain`.
- The UI never calls analyses directly. It talks to an `Engine` (local engine
  now, remote/server engine later), so UI code must not assume results are
  computed in-process or instantly.
- Analysis forms are generated from operation specs. Do not hand-build a form
  for an operation; extend the spec or the form generator instead.

# State and performance

- Unidirectional state: immutable UI state, events in, a view model per screen.
- Long-running work runs in coroutines with progress and cancellation surfaced
  in the UI. Never block the main thread (the browser has only one).
- Genotype grids and large tables must be virtualized (`LazyColumn`/
  `LazyRow` or canvas drawing). Never compose one node per genotype cell.
- Heatmaps and scatter plots draw on `Canvas`; downsample before drawing when
  points exceed the pixel count.

# Look and feel

- Material 3 with the app theme; no hard-coded colors outside the theme.
- Every analysis result should be exportable in the TASSEL 5 text format.
